    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Wastewater has been identified as a potential source of water, energy, and nutrients. Water reuse has become increasingly important in water stressed urban centers searching for new water supplies. The thermal and carbonaceous energy in wastewater has been exploited to reduce the energy footprint for wastewater treatment. Nutrient reuse has recently been explored as a means to supplant conventional fertilizers for turf grass and crop fertilization.\r\nThe coupled ultrafiltration osmotic membrane bioreactor (UFO-MBR) is a novel wastewater treatment technology capable of producing an effluent fit for water reuse applications requiring superior water quality and producing a phosphorus rich stream suitable for nutrient recovery. A trace organic chemical (TOrC) removal study, potential improvements for the UFO-MBR through enhanced draw solutions and a life cycle analysis (LCA)/comparison are presented.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Holloway, Ryan and Maltos, Rudy and Coontz, Jason and Hering, Amanda and Munakata-Marr, Junko and Miller-Robbie, Leslie and Stokes, Jennifer and Cath, Tzahi. (2016). E1.04 Holloway 2016 ReNUWIt Annual Meeting Poster. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/fz217yn3855",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Bell, E. A., Holloway, R. W., & Cath, T. Y. (2016). Evaluation of forward osmosis membrane performance and fouling during long-term osmotic membrane bioreactor study. Journal of Membrane Science, 517, 1-13. http://doi.org/10.1016/j.memsci.2016.06.014 ",
            "type": "citation/reference",
